  "name": "Question 4",
  "problem": "Suppose that $|\\,p\\,|=6$, $|\\,q\\,|=12$ and that the angle between the vectors is $\\theta ={150}^{\u2218}.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p$ in terms of the vector $p.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q=$\n{{field-1}}\n$p$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the scalar projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =|\\,q\\,|\\operatorname{cos}\u2061\\theta  \\\\  & =12\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({150}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the unit vector that is parallel to $p:$\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{p}{|\\,p\\,|}=\\frac{p}{6}=\\frac{1}{6}p\n$$\n\nFinally, we compute the vector projection as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & ={\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q\\cdot u \\\\  & =-6\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6}p \\\\  & =-\\sqrt{3}\\,p\\end{aligned}\n$$",
